Subject: [PATCH] Expose signed PPCIe mode and NVSwitch lock claims

A relying party needs to know that a CC-off Protected PCIe launch is really
in PPCIe mode with locked NVSwitches. NVML and NSCQ report that state from
the host-controlled driver, so it is not evidence.

The signed SPDM opaque data already carries both facts. The GPU verifier
derives m_mode from FEATURE_FLAG but never serializes it, although the CLI
prints x-nvidia-gpu-mode. The switch parser reads SWITCH_LOCK_STATUS but
drops it. Emit both: x-nvidia-gpu-mode as the SDK names it, and the
little-endian lock status as x-dstack-switch-lock-status.

Upstream-Status: Pending

